.TH PART 5
.SH NAME
part \- solid part source and stream
.SH DESCRIPTION
A part source has one statement per line for the programs of a pipe,
.IR extrude (1),
.IR bool (1)
and
.IR fillet (1);
# begins a comment, and
.I "name = expr"
defines a name as in
.IR sm (5).
.I U
and
.I v
are the two axes other than
.IR a ,
in alphabetical order.
.TP
.BI profile " name " along " a u v r"
.RI [ "u v r" " ...]"
.br
.BI corner " u v r"
.RI [ "u v r" " ...]"
.br
A closed outline in the plane across the world axis
.IR a ,
its corners in order, each rounded by an arc of radius
.I r
(sharp for 0); corner lines continue it.
.TP
.BI circle " name " along " a u v d"
A circle of diameter
.IR d .
.TP
.BI extrude " name " from " w0 " to " w1 p"
.RB [ draft
.IR deg ]
.RB [ pattern
.I ax n p
.RI [ "ax n p" ]]
.br
The solid of profile
.I p
from
.I w0
to
.I w1
along its axis.
With a draft (0 to 89 degrees) each side leans inward;
with a pattern,
.I n
copies are made,
.I p
apart along the signed axis, as one solid.
Faces are named
.IB name .start ,
.IB name .end
and
.IB name . p . k
for side
.I k
of the profile.
.TP
.BI union " name a b"
.RI [ c " ...]"
.br
.BI cut " name a b"
.RI [ c " ...]"
.br
.BI common " name a b"
.br
Replace the named solids by the solid
.I name
(their union,
.I a
less the others, or their common part).
.TP
.BI round " r " convex
.br
.BI round " r pattern pattern"
.br
.BI sharp " pattern pattern"
.br
Give a radius to the outward edges, or to the edges between two faces
whose names match the patterns (* for any run of characters).
Of the rules matching an edge, the last applies; sharp is radius 0.
.PP
Each program writes a stream for the next:
.PP
.RS
.nf
PliCad 1
source PATH
brep NAME ... end
@N TEXT
.fi
.RE
.PP
The stream holds the solids so far, and each source line not yet used,
with its line number
.IR n .
.I "Name = expr"
lines are kept for every program.
Lines still unused at the end of the pipe are refused.
.SH SEE ALSO
extrude(1), bool(1), fillet(1), mould(1), tostep(1), measure(1)
